OpenWings patch 0016: retry rate limits and overloads with backoff

Upstream's streaming model path, which every chat and agent reply uses,
retried 502/503/504/529 once after half a second and never retried a 429
rate limit, so a busy hosted provider ended the reply with an error.
OpenManus retries model calls with exponential backoff.

  * src/llm_core.py (_stream_candidate_with_context_recovery): before any
    output, a 429, 503 or 529 is retried up to WINGS_MODEL_RETRIES times
    (default 3), waiting what the provider asks for ("try again in 20s")
    or 2, 4, 8 seconds (1, 2, 4 for overloads), at most 20 seconds each;
    see wings/backoff.py. When the provider asks for longer (an hourly or
    daily quota) there is no retry. The failed stream, and with it the
    local model slot, is closed before the wait. 502, 504, network errors
    and upstream's own "Cannot reach" 503s keep upstream's handling, and
    with several models configured upstream still moves to the next one.

Applies to: odysseus-dev/odysseus@9d0d3720f4ca181d87bef94da826d730acc6d483
